{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tools, languages, and frameworks I reach for — and why."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/releasenotes\/skills"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"title":"Dependencies","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Haydar Karkin"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/Skills"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Over 12 years I’ve built up a stack that I’m genuinely comfortable with,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not just familiar with. Here’s what I use and what I think of each."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Languages","level":2,"text":"Core Languages"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Swift","level":3,"text":"Swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"My primary language. I’ve been writing Swift since the early days and have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"watched it mature into one of the best-designed languages in the industry."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Strong opinions on value types, protocol-oriented design, and the right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use of generics."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Objective-C","level":3,"text":"Objective-C"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Still fluent. Legacy codebases don’t scare me — bridging Swift and ObjC"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in mixed projects is something I’ve done extensively."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"iOS-Frameworks","level":2,"text":"iOS Framew